#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SE2238 expect=noViolation domain=TS
#note "GLPTYP rows carry a GLP-type value that is not an NY term (or are empty, guarded out by non_empty); the NY term 'Y' sits only on the GLPFL parameter, where it belongs -> no violation."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#library codelist-terms NY Y N NA U
dataset TS label="Trial Summary"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col TSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TSPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter Short Name"
col TSVAL    type=Char label="Parameter Value"
---
S1 | TS | 1 | GLPTYP | FDA GLP
S1 | TS | 2 | GLPTYP | OECD GLP
S1 | TS | 3 | GLPTYP |
S1 | TS | 1 | GLPFL  | Y
